AetherKit

Krea schedule and seeded-noise algorithms and their reference fixture values are
derived from the Apache-2.0 Aether prototype and its Aether / Atelier Swift
references. The retained prototype identifies upstream revision
7aff977df6e88005649b13bc63995f75eb4b217b.

Original Aether / Atelier sources are copyright their respective contributors.
The accompanying LICENSE preserves the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Sample model bundle: AetherKit publishes one set of weights, a Core AI conversion
of Qwen3-0.6B (https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B, revision
c1899de289a04d12100db370d81485cdf75e47ca, Copyright 2024 Alibaba Cloud, Apache
License 2.0), at https://huggingface.co/aether-models/aether-kit-qwen3-0.6b with
that repository's own LICENSE and NOTICE. The weights are not in this
repository; Examples/SampleApp downloads them. AetherKit distributes no other
weights.

This repository contains no model weights, tokenizer files, adapters or
upstream Core AI Models runtime implementation. External assets retain their
own licenses.

H3 geometry, packing, row positions and scheduler conventions are derived from
Aether prototype sources and the pinned Diffusers behavior at commit
7ecb1e1b4fe500be7fb7381a7bb79a24d7fa3941, copyright 2026 The MiniMax and
HuggingFace Teams, licensed under Apache-2.0. The small CPU fixtures retain
original pipeline/oracle values, not model weights. Their source hashes and
scope are recorded in docs/evidence/h3-cpu-readiness-2026-10-18.json.

Third-party Swift packages, resolved by SwiftPM and not vendored here, are used
only by the optional AetherKreaTokenizers, AetherH3Tokenizers and
AetherFlux2Tokenizers products:

- swift-transformers 1.1.0 (https://github.com/huggingface/swift-transformers),
  Apache License 2.0, copyright Hugging Face.
- swift-jinja 2.5.1 (https://github.com/huggingface/swift-jinja), Apache License
  2.0, copyright Hugging Face.
- swift-collections 1.7.3 (https://github.com/apple/swift-collections), Apache
  License 2.0 with Runtime Library Exception, copyright Apple Inc. and the Swift
  project authors.

FLUX.2 [klein] schedule, rotary layout, prompt rendering, reference-image
positions and bundle recipe are derived from the Apache-2.0 Aether prototype
(spec 11 Part B, recipes/flux2-klein-4b*.toml) and observed behavior of the
pinned black-forest-labs/FLUX.2-klein-4B checkpoint at revision
e7b7dc27f91deacad38e78976d1f2b499d76a294 (Apache-2.0) through unmodified
Diffusers 0.37.1. No weights or fixtures are distributed; local exports keep
the checkpoint's LICENSE.md beside the assets.

Kokoro speech export graphs (Forge/kokoro) reimplement forward passes of the
kokoro 0.9.4 package (https://github.com/hexgrad/kokoro, Apache-2.0), itself
adapted from StyleTTS 2 / iSTFTNet (https://github.com/yl4579/StyleTTS2, MIT),
and are checked against the pinned hexgrad/Kokoro-82M checkpoint at revision
f3ff3571791e39611d31c381e3a41a3af07b4987 (Apache-2.0). No weights, voices or
reference audio are distributed; the model card attributes CC BY 3.0 (Koniwa)
and CC BY 4.0 (SIWIS) training audio. AetherSpeech includes no
grapheme-to-phoneme code and no espeak-ng (GPL-3.0); see docs/kokoro-speech.md.

The Granite 4.0-H hybrid decoder in Forge/language/granite_hybrid.py and the reduced
SSD stack in Spikes/hybrid-state-003/q1_repro.py (development tooling and a defect
repro, not part of any product) follow the GraniteMoeHybrid architecture as
implemented in Transformers 4.57.3 (https://github.com/huggingface/transformers),
Apache License 2.0, copyright The HuggingFace Team and IBM: layer structure,
multipliers and the Mamba-2 SSD maths. They are written for AetherKit, not copied.
The checkpoint, ibm-granite/granite-4.0-h-350m at revision
3b17b717b8f2f5d305b0a92c1491e239aeda19c8, is Apache-2.0 and is not distributed.
